From: =?UTF-8?q?Eduardo=20Garc=C3=ADa-M=C3=A1dico=20Portabella?=
 <woodyst@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 11 Jul 2026 16:35:01 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 001/106] arm64: dts: qcom: sm7150-xiaomi-common: fix USB-C to
 allow real charging

The typec connector was configured power-role=source only, so the port
never negotiated as a sink and charging silently failed (it would even
back-feed a connected powerbank instead). Switch to power-role=dual and
add the required sink-pdos/op-sink-microwatt.

Deliberately capped to a 5V-only sink-pdos: this board's SMB5 charger
only has a native 5V input path, and the earlier attempt at also
advertising a PDO_VAR up to 12V made TCPM negotiate 12V, which SMB5
then rejected as an overvoltage (USBIN read 0V/0A) instead of falling
back to 5V.

Verified on real hardware (POCO X3 NFC / surya): port now shows
power_role "source [sink]", port_type "[dual] source sink", and
pm8150b-charger reports real charging current.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi | 13 ++++++++++++-
 1 file changed, 12 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
index 3209faf98..ee13797fc 100644
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sm7150-xiaomi-common.dtsi
@@ -601,13 +601,24 @@ &pm6150_typec {
 	connector {
 		compatible = "usb-c-connector";
 
-		power-role = "source";
+		op-sink-microwatt = <10000000>;
+		power-role = "dual";
 		data-role = "dual";
 		self-powered;
 
 		source-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
 			       PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
 
+		/*
+		 * No BQ2597x charge-pump driver/DT node exists yet, so this
+		 * board can only actually charge through the SMB5 5V path.
+		 * Advertising higher PPS/AVS voltages (e.g. 12V) makes TCPM
+		 * negotiate them, which SMB5 then rejects as an overvoltage
+		 * (USBIN reads 0V/0A) instead of falling back to 5V.
+		 */
+		sink-pdos = <PDO_FIXED(5000, 3000, PDO_FIXED_DUAL_ROLE |
+			     PDO_FIXED_USB_COMM | PDO_FIXED_DATA_SWAP)>;
+
 		ports {
 			#address-cells = <1>;
 			#size-cells = <0>;
